        {
            "Section": "IT.LBCAT",
            "Unnamed: 1": "LBCAT",
            "Unnamed: 2": "What was the name of the lab panel?\nLab Panel Name [en]",
            "Unnamed: 3": "text",
            "Unnamed: 4": 1,
            "Unnamed: 5": "No",
            "Unnamed: 6": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 7": 8,
            "Unnamed: 8": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 9": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 10": "LBCAT [en]",
            "Unnamed: 11": "LBCAT [CDASH]\nRecord the lab test category, if not preprinted on the CRF. [completionInstructions]\nSponsor-defined controlled terminology. This would most commonly be either a heading or a preprinted category value on the CRF, and not a question to which the site would provide an answer. If a question is asked, the response would typically be a sponsor-defined codelist. If the form is laid out as a grid, then words such as \"Category\" can be included as the column header. Laboratory tests have commonly recognized categories and subcategories that should be used whenever appropriate. LBCAT and or LBSCAT should be included if lab status (NOT DONE) is collected for each lab category/subcategory (e.g., HEMATOLOGY, CHEMISTRY, URINALYSIS). [implementationNotes]\nMaps directly to the SDTMIG variable listed in the column with the heading SDTMIG Target. [mappingInstructions]\n[Lab Panel Name]; NULL [prompt]",
            "Unnamed: 12": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 13": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 14": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 15": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 16": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 17": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 18": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 19": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 20": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 21": NaN
        },
        {
            "Section": "IT.LBPERF",
            "Unnamed: 1": "LBPERF",
            "Unnamed: 2": "Was the sample collected? [en]",
            "Unnamed: 3": "text",
            "Unnamed: 4": 2,
            "Unnamed: 5": "Yes",
            "Unnamed: 6": "CL.C66742.NY.NY",
            "Unnamed: 7": 3,
            "Unnamed: 8": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 9": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 10": "LBPERF [en]",
            "Unnamed: 11": "LBPERF [CDASH]\nIndicate whether or not lab specimen was collected or measurement performed. [completionInstructions]\nThis may be implemented for an Lab entire panel, or on a specific lab test basis. General prompt question to be used as a data management tool to verify that missing results are confirmed missing. [implementationNotes]\nThis does not map directly to an SDTMIG variable. May be used to derive a value into the SDTMIG variable LBSTAT. If the CDASH variable LBPERF = \"N\", the value of LBSTAT will be \"NOT DONE\". If LBPERF = \"Y\", LBSTAT should be null. A combination of SDTMIG variables ( e.g., LBCAT and LBSCAT, LBTPT ) is used to indicate that multiple tests were not done. In this situation, the SDTMIG variable LBTESTCD would be populated as LBALL and an appropriate test name (LBTEST) provided. See SDTMIG v3.2 Section 4.1.5.1.2. [mappingInstructions]\nLab Performed; Sample Collected [prompt]",
            "Unnamed: 12": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 13": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 14": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 15": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 16": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 17": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 18": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 19": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 20": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 21": NaN
        },
        {
            "Section": "IT.LBDAT",
            "Unnamed: 1": "LBDAT",
            "Unnamed: 2": "What was the date of the lab specimen collection?\nCollection Date [en]",
            "Unnamed: 3": "date",
            "Unnamed: 4": 3,
            "Unnamed: 5": "No",
            "Unnamed: 6": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 7": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 8": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 9": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 10": "LBDAT [en]",
            "Unnamed: 11": "LBDAT [CDASH]\nRecord the date when specimen collection was done using this format (DD-MON-YYYY). [completionInstructions]\nA complete date is expected. The date of collection may be determined from the date of visit (VISDAT) and if so, a separate assessment date field is not required. The SDTMIG LBDTC variable contains either a date/time when a specimen is collected at a point in time or the start date/time, when a specimen is collected over time. [implementationNotes]\nThis does not map directly to an SDTMIG variable. For the SDTM submission dataset, concatenate all collected CDASH DATE and TIME components and populate the SDTMIG variable LBDTC in ISO 8601 format. [mappingInstructions]\nCollection Date [prompt]",
            "Unnamed: 12": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 13": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 14": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 15": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 16": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 17": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 18": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 19": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 20": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 21": NaN
        },
        {
            "Section": "IT.LBTIM",
            "Unnamed: 1": "LBTIM",
            "Unnamed: 2": "What was the (start) time of the lab specimen collection?\nCollection Time [en]",
            "Unnamed: 3": "time",
            "Unnamed: 4": 4,
            "Unnamed: 5": "No",
            "Unnamed: 6": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 7": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 8": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 9": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 10": "LBTIM [en]",
            "Unnamed: 11": "LBTIM [CDASH]\nRecord time of collection (as complete as possible). [completionInstructions]\nMay be required when multiple assessments are done on 1 day or when the timing in relationship to study treatment is required for analysis or a specimen is collected over an extended time period. [implementationNotes]\nThis does not map directly to an SDTMIG variable. For the SDTM submission dataset, concatenate all collected CDASH DATE and TIME components and populate the SDTMIG variable LBDTC in ISO 8601 format. [mappingInstructions]\n[Start] Collection Time [prompt]",
